[N 36-38 Badlands]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Thelsamar and Ironband's dig, then the Badlands: Hammertoe's map, the Mirages crate, Rigglefuzz's buzzards, Agmond and Murdaloc, Theldurin's errand and the Uldaman urns, with the Twisted Fire Totems on the way. Uldaman itself waits for level 40 (chapter 39e).]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 38 for Murdaloc's camp: Stonevault Bonesnappers 39-40 (14 spawns), Stonevault Shamans 40-41 (5), Murdaloc 42 (one, not elite). Everything else wants 35: A Sign of Hope and Mirages need 35, the buzzard wings 33; Dustbelcher Warriors and Mystics are 36-37, Crag Coyotes 35-38, buzzards 35-39. Under 38 when you reach Agmond's skeleton: hand in Find Agmond, take Murdaloc and leave the camp - Murdaloc (739) and Agmond's Fate (704) ride to chapter 39e at 40, and the steps marked "38+" below are skipped. Shaman: the Fire Totems must still all come from this chapter (Storm, Earth, and Fire is handed in in chapter 39, before Uldaman), so under 38 take them from the Dustbelcher Warriors and Mystics at the supply crate
[OC]|cffffffffBadlands|r  -  you start in Ironforge where chapter 34 left you, hearth = Nijel's Point; it moves to Thelsamar here. About 14,300 quest XP at 38+ (8,000 under 38), every quest plain, no grind steps; the one collection is 4 Buzzard Wings (~31%). Skin the Crag Coyotes on the way
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Ironband Wants You! (707) from chapter 27. Shaman: Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358) holds the Water (32) and Air (33) totems; Fire drops here. A Sign of Hope (721) and Solution to Doom (709) are picked up here and ride to Uldaman in chapter 39e
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Training:|r chapter 34 does not train, so the level 34 and 36 ranks are bought at Eldrun before you fly

[OC]|cffffffffIronforge|r  -  Eldrun in the Forlorn Cavern, then the flight master
